within the lesions (white arrowheads in (a)) and fissure distortion with loss of the regularity (white small arrows in (d)).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CRM2010-361265.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>(a)&#x02013;(c): Photomicrographs demonstrate active young fibroblast proliferation (fibrosis) and tumor cells that are entrapped within the central desmoplasia. (d): Photomicrograph shows neoplastic cells spreading along alveolar septa (lepidic growth) with preservation of the alveolar architecture (hematoxylin-eosin stain).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CRM2010-361265.003"/></fig></floats-group></article>